":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7028034","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"68fda50524258d98b123fbcc625e730365d14d1ee17ce78a4a3c3a3a4470f33e","compact":"4430064e0c3f280544a38530e52976fe7a7e5a08cf8b573290f346aa84fa86d4","nasal":"82a518641ef70277549ee571073d8fb2f0f3bae707985025504e9b411c86504d"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-28-35","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":28,"verse":35,"english":"Thereupon the Rākşasas army began to fight with Maruts and they were overwhelmed in the encounter with the stroke of various weapons.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.682,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-28-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7028035","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"81634bb42f0a8b5421a6bdec4c4905f11d9d98af0f75839c3d9ad23daf2067c5","compact":"d6e5e22f4e340d496f889af3d9d96741e8efb80fbdf3ca92b433515d244716ee","nasal":"d6e5e22f4e340d496f889af3d9d96741e8efb80fbdf3ca92b433515d244716ee"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-28-36","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":28,"verse":36,"english":"Some fell down on earth of their carriers in the battle. And they all stood there in a halfsensible mood, some holding the car, some elephants, some asses, some boars, some Piśācamouthed animals and some embracing the Pannagas. And other night-rangers, having their bodies sundered by the deities gave up their being. The Rakşasas being slain and lying down on earth the action appeared wondrous like a painting.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.636,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-28-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7028036","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f674d051edc0d33c47c7bbdf2b208f46ac7f8959f2284c56a24de2e772aba014","compact":"7a657a891c4b65abe48df5136b4fd5f6e13fc39ae4333e9fce3de05912ee74b5","nasal":"9